    52	**ABSTRACT**
    53	
    54	
    55	Modern software is often implemented in multiple interacting programming languages. When performing static analysis of such
    56	software, it is desirable to reuse existing single-language analyses
    57	to allow access to the results of decades of implementation effort.
    58	However, there are major challenges for this approach. In this
    59	paper, we analyze them and present AXA, an architecture that
    60	addresses them and enables cross-language analysis by integrating
    61	single-language analyses.
    62	To evaluate AXA, we implemented a cross-language points-to
    63	analysis for Java applications that interact with native code via
    64	Java Native Interface (JNI) and with JavaScript code via Java’s
    65	ScriptEngine . The evaluation shows that AXA enables significant
    66	reuse of existing static analyses. It also shows that AXA supports
    67	complex interactions and significantly increased recall of reused
    68	analyses without compromising precision.
